A||||5||sqoach||Never ending problems with my 86 SC||||11||
Z||000000||sqoach||04-02-2001||11:32 PM||||You knew I was gonna post about my problems again, didn't you? Of course you did! Anyway, same old problem still: Overheating. I'm getting the muffler looked at tomorrow and it's gonna get replaced. There's a small hole in it. And water is spitting out of that hole and the tail pipes. I know there will be some water, but this seems like quite a bit. I'm also getting a code 34. Any relation with the hole in the muffler? All of my hoses are connected, so I don't know what to do about that. And now my car is overheating more often than it use to. It still does ok right after I burp the system, but it overheats the next day. My fan kicks on when it's suppost to now. But my temp just skyrockets so fast that it has little effect on the temp. And every time I burp the system, I try real hard to get all the air out. I'm also going to have the radiator looked at. It may be clogged up.<P>And I guess I'll go ahead and go through what I've done so you won't ask later. New caps on both ends (16 lb non-vented radiator cap); new 180^ stat (yes it works); new 195^ fan switch from rodney; water pump works (replaced in november (metal imellars)); burped the system many times; flushed out the system in October (not sure how good of a job I did); hoses are not collapsed or crushed that I'm aware of (I've checked pretty good); no coolant leaks. I think I've covered everything.<P>Maybe the exhaust has something to do with the overheating? Water in the exhaust could mean head gasket going bad? Compression test checked out ok, though. All between 130-140.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily overheating)||||reg||11
